 158: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
 159:     """
 160:     Draw the marker-colored route through the centers of all doors in the parallel wall maze.
 161: 
 162:     Input structure:
 163:     - The grid has a background, parallel full-span walls, one three-pixel door
 164:       segment in each wall, and two marker pixels sharing a color.
 165:     - Walls are either all vertical or all horizontal, and the markers are on
 166:       opposite outer sides of the wall set.
 167: 
 168:     Rule:
 169:     - Keep the scene unchanged except for the route.
 170:     - Visit the door centers in wall order from the upper/left marker side to
 171:       the lower/right marker side.
 172:     - In each corridor, draw an orthogonal path to the cell just before the next
 173:       wall, move along that wall to the door center, cross the center, and
 174:       continue to the next corridor; after the last door, connect to the other
 175:       marker.
 176: 
 177:     Key insight:
 178:     - The three-pixel door segments mark the only crossing points through a set
 179:       of parallel walls, so the output is the corridor path threaded through
 180:       those centers.
